From d7c5db3e2478594577d3fc73cf7f283cb5b85d8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lath <lath.solana@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:13:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] lath: a build feature for the one-shot agent over one
 custom provider

Adds the `lath` feature: --no-default-features --features lath builds the `agent -a <alias> -m <message>` path with channels, eval, the gateway and the WASM host out of the dependency graph, and refuses to compile beside a feature that would put a network client, a process spawner or the plugin host back. Every provider family but `custom` is refused at create_model_provider_inner, and a startup walk refuses any other family, fallback, route, kind override, responses wire or -p by name; the legacy custom:<url> form and remote image downloads are refused too. With the feature off nothing changes.
